# Fix: Stop All Attendance API Calls for YouTube/Recorded Videos

## Problem Summary

From the console screenshot, two clear bugs exist for `youtube_recorded` (and `recorded`) class types:

1. **Unnecessary Attendance API calls** — `JOIN`, `PLAY`, `HEARTBEAT`, `BACKGROUND`, `PAUSE` events are being fired by `useAttendanceHeartbeat.ts` even when the provider is `youtube_recorded`. Recorded videos can be watched any number of times and at any time — no attendance tracking is needed.
2. **Video not playing after closing the player** — When the player modal is closed and reopened, the `YoutubePlayer.tsx` (student side) fires a new token expiry timer on every open cycle but also has a lingering state issue (`tokenExpired`, `sessionEnded` not reset when `playerToken` changes).

The fix must **only touch the LMS module** (files under `web_portal/lms/`). No other modules or Firebase should be changed.

